            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FatDogLane"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good, very easy, LOTS of flavor. I added 3 more tbsp of brown sugar (personal pref.) and it needed a tbsp of apple cider vinegar (made a big difference!) My small 2 lb elk roast took about 7 hours on high in order to shred and I had to add about a 1/2 c. water at the end to keep it moist. Be careful with the hot sauce!! The flavors really condense and a few drops made it pretty spicey. I served it on deli rolls, toasted with mayo &amp; parmesean, a slice of provalone and some homemade cole slaw on top....Hubby LOVED it!"
          },
